 "title": "Auditor's Office / Pike County, Indiana",
 "text": "Auditor's Office / Pike County, Indiana\nSkip over navigation\nPike County, Indiana\nSearch\nSubmit\nMenu\nHome\nGovernment  Boards & Commissions\nCounty Commissioners\nCounty Council\nCounty Officials  Assessor's Office\nAuditor's Office\nClerk's Office\nProsecutor's Office\nRecorder's Office\nSheriff's Office\nSurveyor's Office\nTreasurer's Office\nDepartments  Health Department\nHighway Department\nParks & Recreation Department\nProbation Department\nPurdue Extension, Pike Co.\nSoil & Water Conservation District\nSolid Waste Department\nVeteran's Services Office\nPublic Safety  E911\nEMA\nEMS\nSheriff's Office\nTaxes\nCommunity\nHow Do I?  Browse County Staff\nFind an Event\nFind a Location\nFind a Service\nView FAQs\nView a Slideshow\nVisit the Meeting Center\nFind a Document  Agendas\nBreaking News\nForms & Applications\nMinutes\nNews & Notices\nUseful Links\nStart Content\nAuditor's Office\nHome\nGovernment\nAuditor's Office\nThe Auditor's Department\nThe Auditor's Department is responsible for filing all Homestead Deductions, Mortgage Exemptions, Sales Disclosures, and eligibilities for other property tax deductions: age related, disabilities, and Veterans.\nThe Auditor’s office completes all property transfers via deeds and other acceptable documents. The office gathers the property assessments and submits them to the state of Indiana.\nThe Auditor’s Office maintains the records of the actions of the Pike County Council, the county’s fiscal body.\n********* 2026 Treasurer's Tax Sale (ONLINE) October 14, 2026 10:00 a.m. (ET) - 3:00 p.m. (ET)*********\nOnline registration starts September 14, 2026 8:00 a.m. (ET) - October 13, 2026 12:00 p.m. (ET)\n2026 Treasurer Tax Sale o nline registration www.zeusauction.com\n******** The last day for Redemption from the 2025 Tax Sale is October 27, 2026 at 4:00 PM EST. ********\nAuditor Staff:\nJudith Gumbel - Auditor\nAudra Warner - Chief Deputy\nMisty Brenton - Deputy - Claims\nVacancy - Deputy - Property Mapping\nAmy Ropp - Deputy - County Receipts, Tax Sale, and Excise\nDenise Stillwell - Deputy - Payroll\nRecent News\nUseful Links\nRecent News\n2026 Treasurer Tax Sale Advertisement #3\n2026 Treasurer Tax Sale Advertisement #2\nChanges Regarding Property Tax Deductions\n2025 SRI Certificate Sale Advertisement #3\nAuditor's Office Deputy Position Opening-Filled\nUseful Links\n2026 Treasurer Tax Sale Advertisement #3\n2026 Treasurer Tax Sale List\n2026 Treasurer Tax Sale Advertisement #2\nSBS Portal Link-Transfer Books\n2025 SRI Treasurer Sale Advertisement #3\nMore Useful Links\nContact Us\nJudith Gumbel ,\nAuditor\nPike County Courthouse\n801 E Main St\nPetersburg, IN 47567 Get Directions\nPhone: (812) 354-6451\nEmail Us\nStaff Directory\nHours: M - F 8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.\nIn this Department\nBack to Auditor's Office\nCounty Council\nClaims\nCounty Receipts\nDeeds, Mortgages, Tax Deductions, Homesteads\nPayroll\nProperty Mapping\nTax Sales\nProperty Search\nJump to a division Make a Selection County Council Claims County Receipts Deeds, Mortgages, Tax Deductions, Homesteads Payroll Property Mapping Tax Sales Property Search Section Home\nMore Information\nFind content and services related to this page.\nDocument Center Breaking News\nNews & Notices\nUseful Links\nJump to a content archive Make a Selection Document Center\n- News & Notices\n- Useful Links\n- Breaking News\n© 2026 Pike County, Indiana\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCore Business Technologies",
